<html><head><title>How to Create</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><h1 style="margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; line-height: 1.4; font-size: 32px;"><p class="MsoNormal" style="font-weight: 700;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><span style="font-size: 18pt;">How to assess</span><o:p></o:p></font></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style=""><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">Assessment in transdisciplinary education is not straightforward: discuss all the different options and any imposed limitations with relevant stakeholders before deciding on an approach. This guide presents various methods to evaluate learning outcomes, even in the unpredictable context of transdisciplinary learning. Discover useful tools and insights to ensure fair and high-quality assessments that benefit both students and other participants.</font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style=""><font color="#000000"><br></font></p><p class="MsoNormal" style=""><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">In education, learning is assessed and evaluated, in order to:<o:p></o:p></font></span></p><ul type="disc" style="margin-top: 0cm;"><li class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">Guide the learning process towards cetain goals and outcomes;<o:p></o:p></font></span></li><li class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">Determine whether the learning outcomes or goals have been achieved;<o:p></o:p></font></span></li><li class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">Award certificates or diplomas.<o:p></o:p></font></span></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style=""><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">Learning in transdisciplinary education is unpredictable and varied, making assessment a challenge. It requires a critical look at who the assessment is for, what it should lead to, what the learning outcome is, and how to ensure the quality of the assessment (Gulikers, 2022).<o:p></o:p></font></span></p><ul style=""><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 15.4667px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">Who:</span>&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">in transdisciplinary education, you strive for equality among participants. Since assessment and evaluation primarily focus on the student, this can complicate the equal collaboration between students and other participants. Although little is known about specific strategies to overcome this struggle, it is important to be aware of the role that assessment plays in maintaining equitable collaboration.<o:p></o:p></span></font></li></ul><ul style=""><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 15.4667px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">Purpose:</span>&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">do all students need to learn and develop the same things? Personal, professional, and identity development will vary. Assessment should encourage students to get the best out of themselves, rather than hold them back. This requires ‘assessment for learning’ (Schellekens et al., 2021), allowing for development and differences among learners ("assessment for distinctiveness") (Jorre de St Jorre &amp; Oliver, 2018).<o:p></o:p></span></font></li></ul><ul style=""><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 15.4667px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">What:</span>&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">learning outcomes should focus on the processes all students go through and allow for learning surprises: the unexpected learning experiences (Baggen et al., 2022; Gulikers &amp; Oonk, 2019). Therefore, spend time and attention clarifying the success criteria, preferably together with students.<o:p></o:p></span></font></li></ul><ul style=""><li style="text-indent: -18pt;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 15.4667px; font-family: Symbol;">·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;">How:</span>&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">try to change your view on the quality of assessment. Employ various methodologies and involve students and evaluators in designing them to ensure a reliable perspective (Van der Vleuten et al., 2012).<o:p></o:p></span></font></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style=""><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 21.6533px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">An important competency in transdisciplinary education is 'boundary crossing,' or bridging boundaries. The&nbsp;<a href="https://edepot.wur.nl/568501" style="">BC-rubric</a>&nbsp;(Gulikers &amp; Oonk, 2019) based on this competency helps shaping an assessment framework.</font></span></p></h1></body></html>